{"id":"karakoram-highway","title":"Karakoram Highway","who":"Classic route · Pakistan to the Chinese border","when":"May to October","vehicle":"Car or 4x4 (or motorcycle), 7–10 days","kind":"car","color":"#0f766e","summary":"The \"eighth wonder of the world\": a highway cut through the Karakoram from Islamabad past the Indus gorges, Nanga Parbat and Rakaposhi to the apricot orchards of Hunza, the Passu Cones and the Khunjerab Pass at about 4,700 m. Landslides happen; mountain welcome is famous.","sources":[{"label":"Tribune: my road trip to Khunjerab and Skardu via the KKH","url":"https://tribune.com.pk/article/68892/my-road-trip-to-khunjerab-and-skardu-via-the-engineering-marvel-that-is-the-karakoram-highway"},{"label":"South China Morning Post: the KKH's ups and downs","url":"https://amp.scmp.com/magazines/post-magazine/travel/article/3254603/pakistans-karakoram-highway-ups-and-downs-taking-8th-wonder-world-stunning-views-welcoming-people"}],"approximate":"Main stops; the line follows the highway.","km":870,"bbox":[72.8113,33.6301,75.4598,36.8764],"stops":[{"name":"Islamabad","place":"Islamabad, Pakistan","at":[33.6938,73.0652],"text":"The capital under the Margalla hills.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Ali_Mujtaba_WLM2017_FAISAL_MOSQUE_019.jpg/500px-Ali_Mujtaba_WLM2017_FAISAL_MOSQUE_019.jpg","page":"Faisal Mosque","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ali_Mujtaba_WLM2017_FAISAL_MOSQUE_019.jpg","credit":"Ali Mujtaba","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}},{"name":"Abbottabad","place":"Abbottabad, Pakistan","at":[34.1436,73.2133],"text":"Pine hills where the KKH begins.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/Abbottabad_City_view.jpg/500px-Abbottabad_City_view.jpg","page":"Abbottabad","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Abbottabad_City_view.jpg","credit":"Wasim 5560","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}},{"name":"Besham","place":"Besham, Pakistan","at":[34.9292,72.879],"text":"Into the deep Indus gorge.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Nanga_Parbat_Indus_Gorge.jpg/500px-Nanga_Parbat_Indus_Gorge.jpg","page":"Indus River","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nanga_Parbat_Indus_Gorge.jpg","credit":"Heavyrunner","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0"}},{"name":"Chilas","place":"Chilas, Pakistan","at":[35.4195,74.0963],"text":"Ancient rock carvings by the road; Nanga Parbat views at Raikot."},{"name":"Gilgit","place":"Gilgit, Pakistan","at":[35.9208,74.314],"text":"Past the meeting of three great ranges.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Gilgit_City_a_View_from_Gilgit_serena_hotel.jpg/500px-Gilgit_City_a_View_from_Gilgit_serena_hotel.jpg","page":"Gilgit","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gilgit_City_a_View_from_Gilgit_serena_hotel.jpg","credit":"Fehd.raza @fehd.raza","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}},{"name":"Hunza (Karimabad)","place":"Karimabad, Hunza","at":[36.3271,74.6593],"text":"Baltit fort, apricot trees and Rakaposhi across the valley.","source":{"label":"Tribune","url":"https://tribune.com.pk/article/68892/my-road-trip-to-khunjerab-and-skardu-via-the-engineering-marvel-that-is-the-karakoram-highway"},"photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/Baltit_fort%2C_Hunza_Valley.jpg/500px-Baltit_fort%2C_Hunza_Valley.jpg","page":"Baltit Fort","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Baltit_fort%2C_Hunza_Valley.jpg","credit":"MuhammadUsama25","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}},{"name":"Passu","place":"Passu, Pakistan","at":[36.4658,74.8943],"text":"The jagged Passu Cones and a famous swaying bridge.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e5/Pasu_cones.jpg/500px-Pasu_cones.jpg","page":"Passu","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pasu_cones.jpg","credit":"Mehrunisa Reimoo","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}},{"name":"Khunjerab Pass","place":"Khunjerab Pass","at":[36.8501,75.4283],"text":"The borde